# HB-NONE (remake phase 1, 2026-10-11): the generated hitboxes were removed on purpose; animation, sound, movement and timing stay.
# The owner authors this move's hitbox by hand in the Workbench; its strike window is gameplay.json "strike" (timing metadata only).
# Instant Transmission roll forward (phase 4, owner 2026-10-11: "like Mewtwo"; the XV2 sequence of skill 001_GOK_KUR, REMAKE-P1.md "The XV2 Instant Transmission sequence").
# Timing and intangibility from Mewtwo's own roll measured in this engine: 37 frames, intangible f5-22. The clip chain (ESC_KUR vanish, reappear) is the row; the body is
# hidden and intangible for the gap, and the row's root path carries it forward. Sounds at XV2's BAC frames: (no voice line: XV2 plays VOX cue 55 here, deliberately dropped on a roll), the common swing (CMN cue 40) at 3,
# the skill's own SE (KUR cue 0) at 15. The wind-streak effect (common effect 42, frame 10) is bound by animation row in fx_bindings (tools/build.py ROW_FX).
# A forward roll turns him round as he reappears (Melee: Mario and Mewtwo end a forward roll facing the other way; a back roll and the spot dodge keep the facing).
# No ki cost; no hitbox.
PUT ANIM_RATE 1.0
wait_until 3
sfx behavior=1 sfx_id=200145 volume=100 panning=64
wait_until 5
body_state state=2
PUT HIDDEN 1
wait_until 15
sfx behavior=1 sfx_id=200148 volume=127 panning=64
wait_until 23
PUT HIDDEN 0
PUT FACING 0
body_state state=0
wait_until 34
iasa
